<title>UK: United off on rival TV consortium.</title>
<headline>United off on rival TV consortium.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in United News &amp; Media tumbled after British Sky Broadcasting, Carlton Communications and Granada Group Plc announced plans to link up in a bid for digital television licences in the UK, dealers said.</p>
<p>By 0957 GMT, United News shares were down 13p to 699p in a generally firmer market.</p>
<p>Shares in BSkyB, Carlton and Granada, meanwhile, soared and were among the FTSE 100's best performers.  </p>
<p>The group said British Digital Broadcasting, the new venture, plans to offer 15 subscription channels from its three members and the British Broadcasting Corp  BBC.CN to broadcast</p>
<p>One market maker noted heavy switching out of United shares.</p>
<p>&quot;United News is looking left out,&quot; said another.</p>
